---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="About & Contact - Claire Nyquist"
    description="Minneapolis-based data visualization designer, developer, and public health analyst. Specializing in interactive data visualizations using R, Python, JavaScript, and D3. Contact for collaboration opportunities."
>
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8">
        <!-- Hero Section -->
        <div class="text-center mb-16">
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">
                About & Contact
            </h1>
            <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto mb-16">
            <!-- About Section -->
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-12 items-start">
                <!-- Headshot Image -->
                <div class="lg:col-span-1">
                    <div class="relative">
                        <img
                            src="/images/headshot.png"
                            alt="Painted portrait of Claire Nyquist"
                            class="w-full h-auto object-contain rounded-lg shadow-lg"
                        />
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- About Content -->
                <div class="lg:col-span-2">
                    <div
                        class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6"
                    >
                        <p>
                            I live at the intersection of <em
                                >How does this virus work?</em
                            > and <em
                                >How can I make this spreadsheet accessible?
                            </em>
                            <p></p> With a Master of Public Health from the University
                            of Minnesota and First Class Honors in Graphic Communication
                            Design from the University of Westminster in London, I've
                            spent my career translating complex science into actionable
                            insights.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            I've worked in a pediatric ER, veterinary diagnostic
                            lab, and as a federal consultant. From HTML/CSS to
                            JavaScript and R, I build digital experiences that
                            are accessible, functional, and statistically sound.
                            I've also spent my free time volunteering at the
                            Minneapolis Institute of Art and The Bakken Museum.
                            I organize tcplot (our local Twin Cities data-viz
                            community). I aim to spark curiosity&mdash;whether
                            you are five years old or a federal policymaker.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Want to collaborate on a project that requires both
                            a microscope and a paintbrush? Get in touch at
                            clairenyquist@gmail.com.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
